dosbox-automation: keep Joliet names longer than mkisofs' 103-character
'-joliet-long' limit. The directory record's length check above bounds
the name; the path buffer is bounds-checked since 3.8.8 (750e8d7b).
Torture test gap G17: discs authored on Windows carry names up to 110
characters, which were cut and lost their extension.

--- a/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_iso9660.c	2026-10-16 18:40:52.498435062 +0200
+++ b/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_iso9660.c	2026-10-16 18:40:52.514435150 +0200
@@ -1901,12 +1901,12 @@
 
 	if (iso9660->seenJoliet) {
 		/* Joliet names are max 64 chars (128 bytes) according to spec,
-		 * but genisoimage/mkisofs allows recording longer Joliet
-		 * names which are 103 UCS2 characters(206 bytes) by their
-		 * option '-joliet-long'.
+		 * but authoring tools record longer ones: genisoimage/mkisofs
+		 * up to 103 UCS2 characters (206 bytes) with '-joliet-long',
+		 * Windows tools up to what the directory record holds. The
+		 * record already bounds name_len (checked above), so the
+		 * whole name is kept.
 		 */
-		if (name_len > 206)
-			name_len = 206;
 		name_len &= ~1;
 
 		/* trim trailing first version and dot from filename.
